1
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:34,000
I kick a pebble and my shoe flies off too.

3
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:42,320
Onto the head of the
carpenter I was choking,

4
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:48,440
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if you drop your spirit,
Katsushika is there for you.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,600
Even a yawn is no different.

7
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,540
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:10,200
From the water intake
tower with its pointed hat,

9
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:16,800
the sun sets toward the rented shop.

10
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:25,240
Tomorrow will end just like this too,
won't it.

11
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say.

12
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
I only realized it after losing it.

13
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,020
Because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:41,700
Tears of joy! Terai's first rebuilding!

15
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:53,720
It's about lunchtime

16
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:55,820
Guess we'll order katsudon.

17
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:58,280
Ryo-san, order mine too while you're at it.

18
00:01:58,960 --> 00:01:59,780
What, you're being stingy?

19
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:01,400
Aren't you bringing a bento today?

20
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,160
Then you're fine with katsudon too, right?

21
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,680
No, I'll have soba from Mori.

22
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:07,243
Mori soba? Just one plate of Mori soba?

23
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,300
You just got your paycheck, didn't you?

24
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:13,760
The loan payments are brutal. I only
get 5,000 yen a month for pocket money.

25
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,020
Good grief.
Getting married is a real double-edged sword

26
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:22,920
Officer! Officer! Officer!

27
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:23,900
W-what's wrong?

28
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:27,340
I forgot my wallet. I'm in a hurry, officer.

29
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,140
Could you lend me 5,000 yen?

30
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:30,760
5,000 yen?

31
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:34,360
Please! I'll definitely pay you back!
I'm in a hurry! Please!

32
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:43,160
Sorry, really! I'll definitely pay it back!

33
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:44,780
There's no time!

34
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:53,240
That's right! Katsudon and soba
from the Kōen-mae police box!

35
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:56,600
Yō-san, Tanma! Cancel my soba!

36
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:02,160
What? You lent him 5000 yen and
didn't even ask his name or address?

37
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:06,420
He's not from around here, right?
I didn't recognize his face.

38
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:10,320
You idiot, that's basically like
throwing 5000 yen down the drain!

39
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,820
He's definitely not coming back to pay it.

40
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,020
You think so?

41
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:20,500
Listen, in this cutthroat world, the golden rule for
modern people is to treat everyone you meet as a thief!

42
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:21,940
It can't be helped.

43
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:26,020
If "it can't be helped" fixed everything,
we wouldn't need the police!

44
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,840
Just so you know,
I'm not sharing my earnings with you!

45
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:30,180
Mm, yeah.

46
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:35,540
Hey!

47
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:36,640
Hey.

48
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:39,600
Well, if it isn't Mr. Terai and Ryo-san.

49
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:41,720
Thanks for your hard work on patrol.

50
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:44,680
Laid off and with no food,
yet you're walking a dog?

51
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:45,800
Must be nice to be so carefree.

52
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:49,820
I didn't get laid off, I retired.

53
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:51,480
Was that it?

54
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,500
We always run into each other
at the pachinko parlor, though.

55
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:58,000
Don't mind it. We're both in the same boat with no food,
right? Right, Pochi?

56
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:01,540
It's John, right? John!

57
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,260
That tickles, John.

58
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,860
Wow, he's completely taken to Mr. Terai.

59
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:12,440
Terai's always been
popular with dogs and cats

60
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:16,860
Hey there, grandpa and grandma,
how are you doing?

61
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:21,260
Hello, Mr. Matsui, Mr. Kiyohara,
is your back feeling better now?

62
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,140
Mr. Terai.

63
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,500
Mr. Takahashi.

64
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,280
Did you find your lost dentures?

65
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,360
Here you go.

66
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:29,300
Thanks.

67
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:30,000
Goodbye.

68
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:34,320
Hey. Do you even know about
that old lady's dentures?

69
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:35,757
Well, yeah.

70
00:04:35,807 --> 00:04:39,193
Communicating with the
neighborhood residents is important,

71
00:04:39,243 --> 00:04:41,200
and it's for when something happens.

72
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:45,420
When something happens? When exactly
would knowing about dentures come in handy?

73
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:51,300
Wait, there's that dog that barks
at everything down this alley, right?

74
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:52,580
Let's go this way.

75
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:55,940
That dog's been in the hospital with
a cold since the day before yesterday.

76
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,880
Grandma, be careful! Let me do that for you.

77
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,860
Terai, sorry about this.

78
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:12,420
Hey, Terai, we're on patrol!

79
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:14,640
I think it's better than
playing pachinko, though.

80
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:20,900
How are you doing, old lady?

81
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:22,280
Ever since your husband passed away,

82
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,400
aren't you lonely, all by yourself?

83
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:25,800
Well, actually,

84
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:28,500
lately, Genjiro from the third block

85
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,880
has made friends at a tea club

86
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:31,900
and even goes to karaoke with them.

87
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,040
Hey, Grandma,

88
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,800
No way, Terai-san!

89
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,520
you know everything about the neighborhood,
don't you?

90
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:39,600
Speaking of the third block, you know,

91
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,440
you know Kuwata at the tofu shop, right?

92
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:43,740
the one with the big mole

93
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,840
the jovial guy, right?

94
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,900
Honestly, I'm beat.

95
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:54,800
Just going around the
neighborhood took three hours!

96
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,860
Terai's really a community-oriented type,
you know.

97
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:01,780
He stops to chat with every
single person he runs into.

98
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:06,420
It's like in baseball, when there's a runner on base,
you always have to bunt them along.

99
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:09,680
He's a sacrifice-bunt-for-life kind of guy.

100
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:13,100
But that matters a lot for a police officer.

101
00:06:13,591 --> 00:06:17,360
If you ask me,
what's so fun about becoming a cop?

102
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:22,480
The real thrill of being a cop is
nailing a criminal in a flashy arrest!

103
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:27,000
Come to think of it,
has Terai ever arrested a criminal?

104
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,560
I don't recall any, to be honest.

105
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,240
I don't know of any either.

106
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:34,980
Could it be that ever since
he became a police officer,

107
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:38,300
he's never arrested a single criminal?

108
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,420
Achoo!

109
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,260
Maybe I caught a cold.

110
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,440
Hey, big brother, that's not fair!

111
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,840
What? You came along later.

112
00:06:47,060 --> 00:06:49,340
Big brother, you went first yesterday too.

113
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:50,980
Come on, what's the big deal?

114
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:56,660
Keep it down a little!

115
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:04,540
A game where you become a
detective and catch the criminal?

116
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,040
Yeah. This one's pretty hard, actually.

117
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,200
I see, so the criminal is in here.

118
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:13,720
Look at that face.

119
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,900
Speaking of which, Dad,
you're a police officer too, right?

120
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:18,540
Yeah, speaking of which.

121
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:23,180
"Speaking of which"? I've been a cop
since long before you two were born.

122
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:26,740
So you've caught thieves and things before,
right, Dad?

123
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:30,120
How do you feel when you arrest a criminal?

124
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:32,120
A criminal?

125
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:32,720
Yeah.

126
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:36,680
Even so,
I've never had the experience, you know.

127
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,800
You've never done it once?

128
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:43,560
It's not like in games or detective shows,
you know.

129
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:46,360
Well, if I get a chance someday.

130
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:57,420
Listen up. Headquarters has sent us the Theft Unit,
Criminal Record Squad 17, today.

131
00:07:57,420 --> 00:08:03,460
We've received word that Tsuruno 007
is hiding somewhere around Kameari.

132
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:09,140
Last year, Katsushika precinct's arrest
rate fell far behind the other precincts.

133
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:14,020
If we let this Tsuru 007 slip
through our fingers again,

134
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:17,660
it'll be a disgrace to the precinct.
We must arrest him, no matter what.

135
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:18,520
Understood?

136
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,740
Reiko and Nakagawa, you take the south side.

137
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:24,760
Ryotsu and Terai, you check the north side.

138
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:25,720
Yes, sir.

139
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:27,620
Chief?

140
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:29,380
What is it, Ryotsu?

141
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:32,580
If we catch that criminal,
do we get a reward?

142
00:08:34,060 --> 00:08:37,323
Well, if you hit a home run,
you get a home run prize,

143
00:08:37,373 --> 00:08:41,240
and if you turn a double play,
you get a double play prize, right?

144
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:44,740
You idiot! This isn't a game!

145
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:48,395
Ugh, you're no fun.
You just keep yelling like that,

146
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:50,380
and nobody feels motivated.

147
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:53,890
So be generous for once.
If we arrest the criminal,

148
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:57,360
buy everyone a drink or something.
Right, Chief?

149
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:04,420
Very well, if you catch the criminal,
I'll buy you a drink.

150
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:06,600
Yay, Chief, I love you!

151
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:07,800
Let's go, Terai!

152
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:13,240
First, the basics of investigation: questioning people,
Ryo-san.

153
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:16,000
Are we really going to check
every single one of these?

154
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:20,520
The Chief always says that piling
up small efforts is what matters.

155
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:24,640
That's like laying down a sacrifice
bunt with no runners on base.

156
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,660
There has to be a quicker way.

157
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:31,820
It's the usual tissue paper exchange,
as always.

158
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,840
Let's start with that block.

159
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:35,620
That one.

160
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,120
That one?

161
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:42,760
This is the usual Kameari Park police box,
as always.

162
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:46,540
We've come to ask for your cooperation.

163
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:50,180
Everyone in the housing complex,
please show your faces.

164
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:53,140
Is this really how we investigate, Ryo-san?

165
00:09:55,740 --> 00:10:00,460
Anyone who won't show their face will be
treated as a wanted criminal and arrested.

166
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,440
Hey, Terai, is he around?

167
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,080
Um...

168
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,480
Is he here?

169
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:14,980
Mr. Saito from Building 4 got
discharged from the hospital.

170
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:15,580
Right?

171
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:20,120
That's not it!
We're looking for the culprit!

172
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,700
There's no culprit here.

173
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,120
Thank goodness.

174
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:27,200
Yay!

175
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:40,240
Yeah, I've got a great idea! How about this: we just go up to everyone around here and yell,
"You're under arrest!" one after another.

176
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:49,520
Whoever runs off in a panic has to be the culprit. Think it'll work?
Then we'll just hit them with a surprise pickoff throw.

177
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:52,200
Is anyone around here?

178
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:01,180
A suspicious-looking man.

179
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:02,940
Hey! Don't arrest him!

180
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:06,160
He's running, Ryo-san!

181
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,840
He took the bait right away.

182
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,060
Terai!

183
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:11,720
Stop!

184
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:13,480
Terai! This way is the shortcut.

185
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:20,620
Motoki's precious flowers...

186
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:25,580
There, that's better.

187
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,260
Ryo-san?

188
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:37,920
Hold it!

189
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:54,100
Prepare yourself! You're under arrest!

190
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:57,880
Got him! We caught him!

191
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,060
Ryo-san, let me have the handcuffs!

192
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:01,660
Saori...

193
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:06,840
You!

194
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:10,760
Saori... sorry, that didn't hurt...

195
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:15,180
Why, it's Sakonji!
You idiot, why did you run?

196
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:19,626
No, if they'd caught me
buying a Saori figure,

197
00:12:19,676 --> 00:12:21,420
I figured I'd get another earful...

198
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:25,320
Geez, what a troublemaker! Let's go, Terai!

199
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:27,820
Ryo-san, what about over there?

200
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:31,120
That noisy dog's in the
hospital with a cold, right?

201
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:43,200
He was discharged this morning!

202
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,980
Idiot! Say that sooner!

203
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:59,680
If it's come to this, we arrest first
and check if they're the culprit later.

204
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:02,740
Are we really allowed to do this, Ryo-san?

205
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:08,620
Of course we are. Police officers' job is to arrest criminals,
so we have to be a little forceful.

206
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,620
R-really?

207
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:11,800
Let's go!

208
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,220
Eek!

209
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:14,280
Whoa!

210
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:15,860
You're under arrest!

211
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,180
Who cares! The culprit's right here!

212
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:21,340
Um...

213
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,500
He's not, Ryo-san!

214
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:24,620
Alright! Next one!

215
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,080
Eek!

216
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:41,900
Why are we the ones getting arrested?

217
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:44,380
That really went too far.

218
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:46,820
Let's gather information diligently,
Ryo-san.

219
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,740
That old lady knows everything
about the people around here.

220
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:52,160
I'll go ask her.

221
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:54,920
Hey, that's impressive.

222
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,380
Is today the grand reopening?

223
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:13,080
Looks like we have to go.

224
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:16,160
Ryo-san, Ryo-san, I heard something good!

225
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:20,840
Where did they go?

226
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:25,360
And I finally got info on someone
who recently moved around here.

227
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:31,980
This sound really cleanses the heart.

228
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:35,500
Well, this shop owner's a pushover.

229
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:38,000
Why would a cop...

230
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:40,280
No good, not quite.

231
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:46,520
No, the line over here is better after all.

232
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:48,280
No, that one, then?

233
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:50,800
No, it's no good.

234
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:55,740
This cop is bad for the heart.
Quick, while we still can.

235
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:58,800
Hey, wait up!

236
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:01,060
There's still ammo left!

237
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:06,160
No, I just need to use the toilet.

238
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:09,160
You! Crane 0075!

239
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,580
We're busted! We're busted!

240
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:27,600
Honestly,
where could Ryo-san have gotten to?

241
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:31,900
What?

242
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,940
Now!

243
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:41,780
I can't wait!

244
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:42,880
Catch that guy!

245
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:46,700
What are you doing?!

246
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:48,940
Stop!

247
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:52,980
Stop!

248
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:59,720
Damn, he got away.

249
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,940
We were so close, too.

250
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:07,000
It's your fault for dawdling like that.

251
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:13,280
That's why you've never caught a single criminal until now,
you know.

252
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:18,480
What's it like when you arrest a criminal?

253
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:22,480
Even if you ask,
Daddy's never experienced it, so...

254
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:24,580
You've never done it once?

255
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:28,760
I guess it's just impossible after all.

256
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:30,540
For me...

257
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:41,540
Ryo-san, this.

258
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:43,560
What? A ten-yen coin, what about it?

259
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:47,400
This ten-yen coin was
dropped by the culprit.

260
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:51,180
This ten-yen coin with the jagged edges is,
I'm pretty sure,

261
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:56,860
Hey, Grandma,
has anyone new moved around here lately?

262
00:16:56,860 --> 00:17:04,060
Lately, there are two at Kameari Heights over there,
and three in Katsushika across the way.

263
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:08,800
And I think there are
two at Okera-sō in 2-chome.

264
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:17,000
You really know your stuff. Is there
anything else you know about those people?

265
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:19,140
Well, let me see.

266
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:21,000
Oh, right, right!

267
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:24,300
The new person who moved into Okera-sō...

268
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:27,280
I think his name is Tsuruta.

269
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:31,200
You know those old ten-yen
coins with the jagged edges?

270
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,400
Apparently he collects them as a hobby.

271
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:36,180
He said so when he got his change.

272
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:40,680
Th-that's right? Or not?

273
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:43,540
There he is! Terai!

274
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:45,960
That's the guy, Tsuruta, 0075!

275
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,060
Uuuuuh...

276
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:53,840
This is it!

277
00:17:54,660 --> 00:17:56,560
Right, you go around the back.

278
00:17:59,860 --> 00:18:02,740
Mr. Tsuruta, Mr. Tsuruta, it's a delivery!

279
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,700
Yes, I'll open it now.

280
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:06,920
I knew it, you're -

281
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:08,280
Y-you're the one from before!

282
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,600
You're under arrest!

283
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:11,460
He's running, Terai!

284
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:13,340
You're under arrest!

285
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,840
What do you think you're doing?

286
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:19,960
Stop!

287
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:24,680
Stop! Babysitting the Chief! Stop!

288
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,360
W-what?

289
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:29,240
Move! Move! Move! Move! Move!

290
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,440
What the hell is this guy?!

291
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:34,720
Stop! Stop, stop! Like I'd stop
just because someone tells me to!

292
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:45,340
N-no, no, no... this is bad...

293
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:47,680
Damn, did we lose him?

294
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:54,580
I'm slow, and I'm bad at martial arts,

295
00:18:54,580 --> 00:18:58,620
I guess I'm just not cut
out for catching criminals.

296
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:06,180
That's exactly why you've
never caught a single criminal!

297
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:08,500
Come on, pull yourself together, dear.

298
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,520
Daddy, you're pathetic.

299
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,500
Yeah, yeah!

300
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:23,400
What a sorry excuse for a cop.

301
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:26,060
Get off of me, would you?

302
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:36,520
That guy, that guy!

303
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:39,120
Terai, arrest him!

304
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:44,980
I'm arresting Suru-no-Suru-no-Nana too!

305
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:46,020
Whoa!

306
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:49,820
Ugh! I won't let him get away!
I won't let go, even if I die!

307
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:51,420
Yes! Good job, Terai!

308
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:55,360
Did they get you? Terai! This is
Terai's first time arresting a criminal!

309
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:58,080
I can get things done too
when I put my mind to it!

310
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:58,740
Guh!

311
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:00,100
Ugh!

312
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,440
I won't let him get away!
I won't let him get away!

313
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:04,720
Calm down! Terai!

314
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:08,500
He's not a chicken!
Don't strangle him like that!

315
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:11,120
Handcuffs! Put the handcuffs on him!

316
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,180
Right, handcuffs!

317
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:15,420
Ugh!

318
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:19,320
Don't put the handcuffs on his neck!

319
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,400
His hands, too!

320
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:23,180
Right.

321
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,800
It's my first time.

322
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:27,460
Hurry up, he'll die!

323
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:32,320
Serial offender, nationwide wanted,

324
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:34,960
I'm arresting Zel 077.

325
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:42,100
This feeling, as a police officer,
is overwhelming.

326
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:45,780
I have a feeling I'll never
get to experience this again.

327
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:48,000
Let me feel this thrill once more.

328
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:55,860
By nationwide order of the Serial Combat Squad,
we're arresting Pickpocket 007!

329
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:02,680
This refreshing thrill
seeps deep into my heart.

330
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:07,200
Yoichi Terai,
this is the greatest thrill of my life!

331
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,820
Yes, so I can burn this
thrill into my heart forever.

332
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:13,000
About ten more times.

333
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:15,880
Enough already! That's enough!

334
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:18,040
Anyway, we're taking him to the box!

335
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:19,580
We did it, Terai!

336
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,280
Ryo-san

337
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:22,240
Yeah.

338
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:25,900
Looks like the Chief's treating us tonight.

339
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:27,700
Wait, Ryo-san.

340
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:29,700
Since we've come this far,

341
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,520
Whoa, I did it, Ryo-san!

342
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:38,660
Are you satisfied now?

343
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:39,980
Then that's good, right?

344
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:40,780
While we're at it,

345
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:58,660
Wow, well done, Terai-san,
what a fine achievement!

346
00:21:58,660 --> 00:22:01,440
This is the result of your
steady everyday patrolling.

347
00:22:02,180 --> 00:22:04,180
It's nothing that special.

348
00:22:04,180 --> 00:22:06,400
No, just as Nakagawa said.

349
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:10,500
It's because of the thorough patrols you do daily,
staying close to the community,

350
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:12,580
that you were able to arrest the criminal.

351
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:17,300
I really wish someone around here
would take a good lesson from that.

352
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:21,280
Now, now, Chief, today is a happy day.

353
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:25,920
As promised, let's go out and celebrate big time,
on the Chief's treat!

354
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:27,460
Excuse me.

355
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:29,360
It's you from the other day.

356
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:31,060
Thank you for your help the other day.

357
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:32,600
Well...

358
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:37,940
Yes, here's the 5,000 yen I borrowed,
and please share this with everyone.

359
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:39,300
What's going on here?

360
00:22:39,300 --> 00:22:41,780
I never thought he'd actually
come back to return it.

361
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,520
So that's what it was.

362
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:47,460
Well, I'm glad I could be of help.

363
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:50,560
If you're ever in trouble, just stop by.

364
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:55,280
Well, my wife was giving birth then and I was in a panic,
so I really appreciated it.

365
00:22:56,040 --> 00:22:57,540
So, was the baby born safely?

366
00:22:58,080 --> 00:23:00,340
Thanks to you, a healthy baby boy was born.

367
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:02,000
And they're twins, no less.

368
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,940
Wow, that must have been a handful.

369
00:23:03,940 --> 00:23:06,480
So, where do they live,
and what are their names?

370
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:08,360
We named them Kenji and Kouji.

371
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:11,260
Their address is the next corner past
the intersection in the second block...

372
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:13,520
It's that apartment building on the corner.

373
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:14,900
Three arrests is great, but

374
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:17,040
still, that kind of sight

375
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:19,280
really suits Terai-san the most.

376
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:20,100
Really.

377
00:23:20,660 --> 00:23:22,440
Sometimes even a sacrifice bunt

378
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:24,420
can end up being the winning run, you know.

379
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:27,040
But I've always lived my life

380
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:28,980
by the grand slam philosophy!

381
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:32,180
You strike out more often, though.

382
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:33,700
Oh my, oh my, oh my.

383
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:37,480
The chief umpire is Kobe.

384
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:38,960
Beef is delicious, isn't it?

385
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:50,220
Dear, did something good happen?

386
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:51,500
Nothing really.

387
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:53,120
Alright, dinner's ready.

388
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:54,060
Coming!

389
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:20,620
Even in the middle of the night,
calls come in.

390
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:27,420
With you, waking up feels good.

391
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:31,800
Even boring stories

392
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:36,600
warm up my whole body.

393
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:42,460
But I want to see my friends.

394
00:24:42,580 --> 00:24:52,660
I surely want to be loved,
even if it annoys everyone a little.

395
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:58,380
Feeling like we're melting into each other.

396
00:24:58,380 --> 00:25:08,040
I surely want to confess,
but somehow, only in love, I'm timid.

397
00:25:08,900 --> 00:25:15,860
Don't hide everything
behind your bravado anymore.

398
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:26,500
Senpai! Nana Otohime is in a
slump and can't draw manga at all!

399
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:30,500
If this goes on, there'll be a hole in the serialization.
What should we do?

400
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:33,260
You'll draw the manga instead, senpai?

401
00:25:33,660 --> 00:25:35,820
Next time: Ryo-san becomes a mangaka.

402
00:25:35,820 --> 00:25:37,500
That's not what I meant.

403
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,720
Thank you for watching.

